imbridge poll GUIDs: send-poll takes an optional "guid" (a UUID) and creates the poll message with it, like
send-message since 0011-chosen-guids, so a caller that recorded it can tell after a timeout whether the poll went out,
and resend it without a duplicate. The UUID check moves into IMBChosenGuid, which send-link now shares.

